# Optional preferred JSON-RPC endpoint per chain. Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) to use.
# IMPORTANT: every VITE_* value is compiled into the public JavaScript bundle and visible to every visitor.
# Never put a secret here. A provider URL that embeds an API key is exposed to anyone who opens DevTools:
# only use keys that the provider lets you restrict by allowed origin / rate limit, or leave these unset
# and rely on the built-in public fallbacks. Must be https (http allowed for localhost only), without user:pass@.
# VITE_RPC_URL_1=
# VITE_RPC_URL_8453=
# VITE_RPC_URL_42161=
# VITE_RPC_URL_59144=
# VITE_RPC_URL_137=
# VITE_RPC_URL_10=
# VITE_RPC_URL_11155111=

# --- Collections page (OpenSea API v2) -------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-ONLY secret: no VITE_ prefix, so it is never bundled into browser code. Put it in .env.local for
# `npm run dev` (read by vite.config.ts) and in your Vercel project's Environment Variables for deploys.
# Get a key at https://docs.opensea.io/reference/api-keys (instant free-tier keys expire after 7 days;
# for anything lasting, create a full key in opensea.io > Settings > Developer).
# OPENSEA_API_KEY=
# Optional, non-secret: use a different collections endpoint than /api/collections.
# VITE_COLLECTIONS_API_URL=

# --- Wallet ERC-20 balances (Alchemy Token API) -------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-ONLY secret: no VITE_ prefix, so it is never bundled into browser code. Put it in .env.local for
# `npm run dev` (read by vite.config.ts) and in your Vercel project's Environment Variables for deploys.
# Create a key at https://dashboard.alchemy.com and enable the networks you want (Ethereum, Base, Arbitrum,
# Optimism, Polygon, Linea, and Sepolia. Native SOL balance on /wallet uses Solana Devnet.
# Never put this value in a VITE_* variable.
# The same key also serves /api/wallet-nfts (Alchemy NFT API v3, EVM only: Ethereum, Optimism, Polygon, Base, Arbitrum). No new variable is needed.
# It also serves /api/wallet-activity (Alchemy Transfers API: Ethereum, Optimism, Polygon, Base, Arbitrum, Sepolia) and /api/solana-activity, /api/solana-balance and /api/solana-transfer (Solana DEVNET only). No new variable is needed; keep it server-only.
# ALCHEMY_API_KEY=
# Native SOL balance (/api/solana-balance) is Solana DEVNET only. It tries Alchemy's solana-devnet host with this key and,
# if Alchemy rejects it (401/403: the key's Alchemy app does not have the "Solana Devnet" network enabled), falls back to
# the public Devnet RPC https://api.devnet.solana.com (no key). Enable Solana Devnet on the key's app in the Alchemy
# dashboard to use Alchemy. SOLANA_RPC_URL (a mainnet URL in some local .env files) is NOT read by NEXORA; remove it.

# --- Wallet connection (Reown AppKit: MetaMask, WalletConnect, Coinbase Wallet, Solana wallets) ------------
# REQUIRED for wallet connections. This is a PUBLIC project ID (it ships in the browser bundle by design, it is not
# a secret). Create one for free at https://dashboard.reown.com and add your site's domain(s) to its allowlist.
# VITE_REOWN_PROJECT_ID=

# --- TON Testnet Wallet Connection (TON Connect 2.0) ------------------------------------------------
# Optional, public: absolute URL of the TON Connect manifest. Defaults to <origin>/tonconnect-manifest.json.
# For local testing, public/tonconnect-manifest.json defaults to http://localhost:5173 with icon http://localhost:5173/nexora-icon-180.png.
# In production, ensure public/tonconnect-manifest.json specifies your real HTTPS origin and icon URL,
# or set VITE_TONCONNECT_MANIFEST_URL to your hosted HTTPS manifest URL. Must be https (http only for localhost).
# VITE_TONCONNECT_MANIFEST_URL=
#
# Optional, public: TON Center v2 API base URL for TESTNET balance and confirmation tracking.
# Defaults to https://testnet.toncenter.com/api/v2. Must use https (http only for localhost).
# Never put an API key or query parameters in this variable; use a server-side proxy if a keyed endpoint is needed.
# VITE_TON_TESTNET_API_URL=
